index 549bf683a9..fb6cedb8be 100644
--- a/docs/Rust.md
+++ b/docs/Rust.md
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@ sccache includes support for caching Rust compilation. This includes many caveat
 * Compilation from stdin is not supported, a source file must be provided.
 * Values from `env!` require Rust >= 1.46 to be tracked in caching.
 * With `SCCACHE_BASEDIRS`, the values of variables read with `env!` or `option_env!` are hashed with the basedirs stripped, so a crate that bakes `env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR")` into its outputs can get a cache hit from another checkout and use that checkout's path. `SCCACHE_BASEDIRS_VERBATIM_ENV_DEPS=CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR,CARGO_MANIFEST_PATH` hashes those values verbatim, so only the crates that read them are cached per checkout. A procedural macro that reads the variable with `std::env::var` is not covered, as rustc does not list it in the dep-info. Listing `OUT_DIR` would stop sharing every crate that `include!`s generated code.
+* With `SCCACHE_BASEDIRS`, a hit can restore a crate compiled in another checkout, with that checkout's paths in its metadata and debug info. With `SCCACHE_BASEDIRS_REMAP_PATHS=1` in the environment of the compile, sccache passes rustc `--remap-path-prefix` so that these outputs are the same in every checkout. Paths under a basedir that holds the working directory become relative to the working directory, so diagnostics still lead to the files, but the compilation directory in the debug info is `.` and a debugger has to be started in the directory cargo ran rustc in. Other paths under a basedir that holds the output directory, such as the `OUT_DIR` of a crates.io dependency, are written under `/sccache/basedir`, which names no local file. A `--remap-path-prefix` of the build's own takes precedence where both match. Crates that cargo compiles outside the workspace root, such as vendored or crates.io sources under a basedir, are each mapped to `.`, so their file names, e.g. `./src/lib.rs`, do not tell the crates apart. Such compiles are not distributed.
 * Procedural macros that read files from the filesystem may not be cached properly.
 * A procedural macro is identified by its crate metadata, so a change to native code it links, with no change to its Rust source or dependencies, is not seen.
 * Crates compiled with `rustc`'s incremental compilation (by default, in the debug profile, cargo's workspace members and path dependencies, see [The Cargo Book](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/profiles.html#incremental)) are not cached by default. sccache exits with an error when `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=1` is set, unless `SCCACHE_ALLOW_INCREMENTAL=1` is set: then only the incremental crates go uncached.
